<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21920" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impexus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inp-</span></b> ), a, um, adj.
		2. inpexus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>uncombed</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in
			post-Aug. prose). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stiriaque impexis induruit horrida barbis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 366</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput impexa foedum porrigine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 3, 126</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tisiphoneque impexa feros pro crinibus angues,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					1, 3, 69</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tegumen immane leonis Terribili impexum seta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 666</span></i>
			.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, = incultus, <i>unpolished</i>, <i>rude</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antiquitas tristis et impexa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. Or. 20</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
